## Specification (`spec/`)

`spec/` holds the protocol's specification as plain Markdown: actors, assets, validators, transactions and invariants. It is the statement of intent the code is reviewed against. **Read the relevant spec before changing a validator or transaction, and update it in the same change.** If the code and the spec disagree, flag it rather than silently picking one.
{%- endif %}

## The worked example

Every generated project ships the **same** worked example — a **gift card**: a one-shot minting policy that mints a unique token gated by a specific UTxO, plus a `redeem` validator that releases a locked gift when the token is burned. On- and off-chain sides share the same parameter ABI through the blueprint, which is why the project builds and its tests pass out of the box. Use it as the template for real logic; replace it, don't accrete around it.{% if spec %} Its human-readable specification, when present, is under [`spec/`](spec/).{% endif %}

